    "https://csusystem.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fort-Collins-CO/Job-Posting-Title-Interior-Architecture-and-Design---Instructor---Open-Pool_R2026106398-1": {
      "title": "Job Posting Title Interior Architecture and Design - Instructor - Open Pool",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\n\nJob Description Position Summary: The Department of Design and Merchandising seeks applications for spring and fall 2026 part-time, adjunct instructor(s) to teach one or more courses in the Interior Architecture and Design Program. Responsibilities may include teaching required undergraduate courses, serving as internship coordinator and/or industry liaison. It is anticipated that this position would allow for remote work (if desired) and the possibility for continuation through additional semesters based on department and program needs. To learn more about the Department of Design and Merchandising (DM), please visit:  https://www.chhs.colostate.edu/dm Salary Range: $60,000 - $80,000 Essential Job Duties: Teach one or more courses in the Interior Architecture and Design Program. May teach other required undergraduate courses as needed. May serve as internship coordinator and/or industry liaison. Conditions of Employment: Pre-employment Criminal Background Check (required for new hires). Supervision: This position reports to the Department Head of Design and Merchandising. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in architecture, interior design, or environmental design. 2-years industry experience in architecture, interior design, or environmental design. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated success in teaching at college and university. Demonstrated success in developing academic and/or professional development classes. Demonstrated involvement in design industry professional organizations. Application Instructions To apply, please submit the following materials directly to this posting: Cover letter CV or resume Portfolio or work samples optional This is an open pool posting. Applications will be reviewed as hiring needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted by individual faculty members if a suitable opportunity becomes available. This pool will expire on January 31, 2027 